      "id": 1,
      "text": "Petersburg was founded in 1748 at the fall line of the Appomattox River, becoming a legal and commercial hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://historicpetersburg.org/history/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Greek Revival courthouse, built 1837‑1839, still hosts trials while echoing Civil War and Civil Rights moments.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://historicpetersburg.org/history/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Petersburg’s Farmers' Bank, erected in 1817, is one of the oldest bank buildings in the United States.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://historicpetersburg.org/history/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The city’s railroads, first authorized in 1830, made Petersburg a critical supply line during the Civil War.",
